    {
      "id": "b_wb_bridge",
      "name": "wb_bridge",
      "tier": "T1",
      "moduleName": "wb_bridge",
      "description": "Bridge from a Wishbone B4 classic slave port to a simple host bus, one word per transfer. Inputs: wb_cyc, wb_stb, wb_we, wb_sel (4 bits), wb_adr (32), wb_dat_i (32), and from the host bus host_rdata (32) and host_rvalid. Outputs: wb_ack, wb_dat_o (32), host_en, host_we, host_addr (32), host_wdata (32). Registers, all 0 after reset: state (2 bits: 0 IDLE, 1 REQ, 2 WAIT, 3 DONE), we_r (1), addr_r (32), wdata_r (32), rdata_r (32). Outputs, all from registers (nothing depends on an input of the same cycle): host_en = (state == REQ); host_we = (state == REQ) & we_r; host_addr = addr_r; host_wdata = wdata_r; wb_ack = (state == DONE); wb_dat_o = rdata_r. On each rising edge: when rst is 1 every register becomes 0. Otherwise by state: IDLE: when wb_cyc & wb_stb: we_r = wb_we, wdata_r = wb_dat_i, rdata_r = 0 and the address is decoded as follows. The address is valid when wb_adr bits 31:20 equal 12'h300 and bits 1:0 are 0. The window is bits 19:16, with off = bits 15:0: window 0 (control registers) is mapped for every off, host address 32'h3000_0000 | off; window 1 (instruction memory) is mapped when off bits 15:11 are 0, host address = off bits 10:0 zero-extended to 32 bits; window 2 (global memory) is mapped when off bits 15:13 are 0, host address 32'h1000_0000 | off bits 12:0; window 3 (shared memory) is mapped when off bits 15:12 are 0, host address 32'h2000_0000 | off bits 11:0; any other window is unmapped. If the address is valid and mapped, and (the access is a read, or wb_sel is 4'b1111), addr_r takes the host address and the state becomes REQ. Every other access (invalid, unmapped, or a write with wb_sel not 4'b1111) is dropped: addr_r keeps its value and the state becomes DONE (rdata_r is already 0). When wb_cyc & wb_stb is not 1 nothing happens. REQ: the state becomes DONE if we_r is 1 (a write), else WAIT (a read). WAIT: when host_rvalid is 1: rdata_r = host_rdata and the state becomes DONE; otherwise nothing changes. DONE: the state becomes IDLE. So a write takes 3 cycles from the cycle in which it is accepted to the cycle of wb_ack (IDLE, REQ, DONE), a read 4 when the host answers one cycle after the request (IDLE, REQ, WAIT, DONE), and wb_ack is high for exactly the cycle in state DONE.",
